{"name":"Sulwhasoo","deep":true,"image":{"url":"assets/photos/sulwhasoo.webp","credit":"https://jp.sulwhasoo.com/blogs/sulwhasoo-post/sulwhasoo_holiday2026","caption":"Sulwhasoo","source":"Used with permission"},"mentions":0,"casual":{"lead":["Sulwhasoo is a skincare and cosmetics brand launched by South Korea's Amorepacific in 1997. It combines traditional Korean herbal ingredients with modern skincare science, aimed at a smoother, more radiant and healthier-looking complexion.","The name refers to a plum blossom that blooms in the snow. The line is sold across Asia, North America, Europe and Australia, and has featured celebrity ambassadors including Song Hye-kyo, Rose and Tilda Swinton."],"sections":[{"h":"How people use it","paras":["Used as a conventional skincare routine of cleansers, toners, serums, creams and masks applied topically; products vary by line, and a flagship cream is marketed under the Jaum name. Visible results from cosmetics generally build with regular use."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Risks & side effects","paras":["As cosmetics, products can cause irritation or allergy in sensitive people, particularly with botanical extracts and fragrance. Ingredients differ across the range."],"subs":[]}]},"gallery":[{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/240829_Tiffany_%40_Sulwhasoo_POP-UP_Store_29.jpg/960px-240829_Tiffany_%40_Sulwhasoo_POP-UP_Store_29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","full":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a7/240829_Tiffany_%40_Sulwhasoo_POP-UP_Store_29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","title":"240829 Tiffany @ Sulwhasoo POP-UP Store 29","license":"CC BY-SA 2.0","creator":"sublimitas_spes","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:240829_Tiffany_@_Sulwhasoo_POP-UP_Store_29.jpg","source":"Wikimedia Commons"},{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/240829_Tiffany_%40_Sulwhasoo_P