 in 1997.[1] It is marketed as combining Korean traditional herbal ingredients with modern skincare science.[1]","The name refers to a plum blossom that blooms in the snow.[1] Amorepacific, which traces its roots to a 1930s camellia-oil business and was founded as Pacific Chemical in 1945, owns more than 30 brands including Laneige, Innisfree and Mamonde alongside Sulwhasoo.[2]","Brand ambassadors have included Song Hye-kyo (2018), Angelababy (2019), Taeyeon (2021), Rose (2022), Tilda Swinton (2023), Choi Hwa-jung (2024) and Im Yoon-ah (2025).[1]"],"infobox":[["Type","Skincare brand"],["Parent company","Amorepacific"],["Launched","1997"],["Origin","South Korea"],["Name meaning","Plum blossom blooming in snow"],["Markets","Asia, North America, Europe, Australia"]],"sections":[{"h":"Brand","paras":["Amorepacific launched Sulwhasoo in 1997 and positions it around traditional Korean herbal ingredients plus modern science.[1] A flagship cream is promoted under the Jaum name.[1]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Parent company","paras":["Amorepacific began in the 1930s when Madame Dokjeong Yun sold camellia oil in Kaesong; her son Sungwhan Suh took over in 1945 and built the business as Pacific Chemical, and the company took the Amorepacific name in 2002.[2]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Marketing","paras":["The brand uses high-profile ambassadors, listed from 2018 to 2025 across Korean, Chinese and international celebrities.[1]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["No studies found."],"subs":[]}],"lore":null,"timeline":[{"year":"1945","event":"Pacific Chemical founded.[2]"},{"year":"1997","event":"Sulwhasoo introduced by Amorepacific.[1]"},{"year":"2002","event":"Company renamed Amorepacific.[2]"}],"refs":[{"title":"Sulwhasoo - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sulwhasoo","source":"Wikipedia","year":null,"type":"encyclopedia"},{"title":"Amorepacific - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amorepacific","source":"Wikipedia","year":null,"type":"encyclopedia"}],"studies":[],"reddit":[],"forums":[]}